course: dictionary
lesson: 1827
title: The coast
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The coast is the land right next to the sea or ocean. «Most Australians live near the coasts, where it rains more.» The sentence tells you that coasts are places where land meets the sea, and that they can have their own weather.
explain: Context clues help you here. «Near the coast the water gets shallow, the wave slows down and piles up.» Waves get bigger and slower where the water becomes shallow, so the coast is the edge of the land where the sea gets shallow.
explain: Coast can also be a verb. «To coast means to keep moving without pushing or pedalling, like riding a bike downhill.» Read the words around it to check: a rider who stops pedalling and still goes forward is coasting.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The coast is clear» means nobody is watching, so it is safe to go. If your meaning fits the sentence, you are probably right.
fact: The coast is the land right next to the sea or ocean.
fact: Coasts is the plural of coast, and coastline is the line where land meets the sea.
fact: To coast means to keep moving without pushing or pedalling, like riding a bike downhill.
fact: «The coast is clear» means nobody is watching, so it is safe to go.
fact: The sea warms up and cools down slowly, so it makes the climate of coasts milder.
exercise: «Most Australians live near the coasts, where it rains more.» What is a coast? | A tall mountain range far inland | *The land right next to the sea | A kind of boat used for fishing
exercise: «Ella let her bike coast down the hill.» What does coast mean here? | Ride as fast as possible uphill | Stop and push the bike up the hill | *Keep moving without pedalling
exercise: «The coast is clear, so you can go now.» What does this mean? | *Nobody is watching, so it is safe | The sky is bright and cloudless | The sea is clean and clear to swim in
test: «Near the coast the water gets shallow, the wave slows down and piles up.» What happens to a wave near the coast? | It disappears into the sky | It turns into ice and stops | *It slows down and piles up | It moves faster and faster inland
test: Which phrase means on the land next to the sea? | *Along the coast | Above the clouds | Deep in the desert
exam: Which sentence uses coast as a verb? | «Many people walk along the coast.» | «The coast of Spain is very sunny.» | *«Dad let the trolley coast down the slope.» | «The coastline is long and rocky.»
